/Title (If your department aims to process a small number of operations, fixed costs will completely overwhelm the modest marginal gain from drafting a few texts. Deploying autonomous agents for minor administrative tasks makes no economic sense. For low-volume microtasks, conventional or scripted automation remains far more economical than an autonomous agent, at an equivalent level of output quality. An AI safety harness is substantial: it requires industrial-scale volumes or very high-value tasks to pay for itself.)
